1
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:38,997
<i>Are you sure you're not going</i>
<i>to investigate Senator Quintin?</i>

2
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:45,754
You'll gather much stronger evidence

3
00:00:46,337 --> 00:00:48,715
if he still believes you trust him.

4
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:55,472
Looks like we can't count
on our old friend anymore.

5
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,814
So they can attend Chiara's wedding?

6
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:11,780
And what do I get out of it?

7
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:14,074
Just tell me what you want in return.

8
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:16,451
Anything?

9
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,168
<i>Your mom and dad</i>
<i>will walk you down the aisle.</i>

10
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:39,057
Bro, some other time,

11
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,601
come with me the next time
I go on vacation.

12
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:43,186
Europe is beautiful.

13
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:46,773
There are so many places you'd enjoy.

14
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:48,274
All you do is work!

15
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:53,822
<i>Looks like Mr. Senator's</i>
<i>been coming here quite often.</i>

16
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:25,645
<i>Oh my God, that's Senator Quintin!</i>

17
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:35,071
You're bald, Mr. Senator,

18
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:40,034
but it looks like
you're not very clean at all.

19
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:49,043
Do you get what I'm saying now?

20
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:50,837
No. What is it?

21
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,171
Is this a game? Find the difference?

22
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,967
What do you mean, find the difference?

23
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,427
There's only one picture.

24
00:02:58,761 --> 00:02:59,804
What exactly am I supposed to see?

25
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:02,181
I really don't see it.

26
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:05,018
Cocoy, take a closer look.

27
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:08,563
Why is Mr. Senator at the same event

28
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:11,149
as the leader of the Sinigang Cartel?

29
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:15,486
Oh, that's your point? I get it.

30
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:16,738
Who knows?

31
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:19,949
He's a fan of Senator Quintin
and wanted an autograph.

32
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:23,453
You know how politicians are these days.
They're like celebrities.

33
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:28,291
Does he look like
he's carrying paper and pen?

34
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:30,335
He's not a fan.

35
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:38,384
This photo is enough evidence
for us to investigate Senator Quintin.

36
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:41,596
- Are you sure?
- I'm sure.

37
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:42,805
So?

38
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:46,100
Should we tell Sean or Agent Alex?

39
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,019
Me?

40
00:03:48,102 --> 00:03:49,604
I'm still on the fence.

41
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,856
You're talking about
taking on someone powerful.

42
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,358
If we make one mistake,

43
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:57,070
we can kiss our new life goodbye.

44
00:03:57,153 --> 00:04:00,114
And we might end up behind bars again.

45
00:04:00,698 --> 00:04:07,330
I suggest that we gather stronger evidence
to make it all add up.

46
00:04:08,998 --> 00:04:13,294
I know someone
who's an expert on the Sinigang Cartel.

47
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:24,347
Where is she?

48
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:26,266
Here she comes.

49
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:34,899
So, Chiara, are you ready?

50
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:43,366
That's not the right way to act.

51
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:46,411
When I say energy, I mean more energy!

52
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:48,454
Give it your all!

53
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:52,542
As Matt Damon and Robin Williams
said in <i>Dead Poets Society</i>,

54
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:59,924
I don't think Matt Damon
was in <i>Dead Poets Society</i>.

55
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:02,927
I think he was with Robin Williams
in <i>Good Will Hunting</i>.

56
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:19,152
Come on, more energy!

57
00:05:28,202 --> 00:05:31,039
Don't shout. Calm down.
You're too excited.

58
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:32,206
You told me to.

59
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:35,626
Wait a second.

60
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:37,378
Are we waiting for someone?

61
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,213
What?

62
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,765
I brought my maid of honor.

63
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:55,813
Hey, Agent Alex!

64
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,190
- Hey!
- Agent Alex!

65
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:58,649
How are you?

66
00:06:00,443 --> 00:06:01,444
How are you?

67
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:05,114
- You still remember!
- I'll stay here for now.

68
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:08,451
Chiara, sorry I'm late.
I dozed off for a bit.

69
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:11,579
You know me. I need enough sleep
to keep my energy up.

70
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:15,917
Just like they said in <i>Good Will Hunting</i>,

71
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,377
seize the day for our bride, Chiara.

72
00:06:26,427 --> 00:06:27,845
How did she know that?

73
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,222
She just got here, didn't she?

74
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:36,187
Oh!

75
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:39,482
Wow, my husband is still
as strong as ever!

76
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,819
I still have to stay in shape.

77
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:48,407
Sooner or later, we'll get out of here.

78
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:52,453
Hey, Valtrovi. You have a visitor.

79
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:55,456
- The who?
- Who?

80
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:17,895
Are you sure we're bringing her along?

81
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:23,568
Yes. Isn't that the whole point
of having a maid of honor?

82
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:31,325
But you look like a modern

83
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:34,912
and empowered woman who can
make her own decisions in life.

84
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:38,124
You don't need a nosy sidekick.

85
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:40,501
I just wanted another girl
to bounce ideas off.

86
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:45,256
Someone to bounce ideas off?

87
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:46,424
Duh.

88
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:49,385
I can do that too. I'm a woman too.

89
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:50,678
Don't I look like one?

90
00:07:51,387 --> 00:07:53,055
Besides, if I shout,

91
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:54,724
"Ding, here's the stone!"

92
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:59,479
I can transform into the best
sounding board in town.

93
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,611
Oh, well, all right.

94
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:11,574
But be careful, Chiara.

95
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:15,703
Your maid of honor looks like
she has a thing for groomsmen.

96
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:20,500
Her?

97
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:23,503
That's who you'll be asking for advice?

98
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:35,806
Not that I'm trying to badmouth her.

99
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:38,976
Or talk behind her back.

100
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:44,065
But your maid of honor
has absolutely no taste.

101
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:50,613
- All right, I'll stay here.
- Okay, Agent Alex.

102
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,797
Don't tell me
she was talking behind my back.

103
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:23,187
for women who tear down other women.

104
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:29,652
I will fully embrace my role
as your maid of honor.

105
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:30,945
I'll always be honest with you,

106
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,739
and I'll keep an eye on everything.

107
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:36,158
And most importantly,

108
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:41,289
I'll tame that feisty
wedding planner of yours.

109
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:45,585
Don't worry about her anymore.

110
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:47,503
I'll handle her.

111
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:51,340
You shouldn't stress yourself out.

112
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:52,967
You know what happens
when you're stressed?

113
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:56,178
Your face starts looking like that.

114
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,974
And you don't want that face
on your wedding day.

115
00:10:01,058 --> 00:10:02,476
That's harsh!

116
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,313
Get ready for my harsh side.

117
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:07,398
I'm going to serve her some harsh browns.

118
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:11,485
Hey!

119
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:12,403
You two,

120
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:15,823
are you coming, or are we waiting
until the end of time?

121
00:10:15,906 --> 00:10:16,741
Let's go!

122
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:19,869
- Let's go.
- Move it! Let's go!

123
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:30,755
Can you move?!

124
00:10:30,838 --> 00:10:32,798
She'll sit beside us, not in front.

125
00:11:28,729 --> 00:11:31,357
You said, "Closer."

126
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:40,991
What brings you here?

127
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:46,956
We need your help.

128
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:58,217
Who's that?

129
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:02,388
That's Mr. Quintin.

130
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:06,016
He's one of the country's senators.

131
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:12,481
Did you match with him on Bumble?

132
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:20,239
They're just exhausting.

133
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:23,200
You keep going on date after date,

134
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:26,996
then you're back to square one
when it doesn't work out.

135
00:12:27,663 --> 00:12:30,499
It's so hard to start all over again,

136
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:33,169
especially after all
those deep conversations.

137
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:35,254
You know,

138
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:37,089
you go from asking,

139
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:43,137
to asking, "What's your favorite color?"

140
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,972
It's rough, isn't it?

141
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:46,807
You know,

142
00:12:47,391 --> 00:12:50,436
I've never used dating apps,
so I can't relate.

143
00:12:57,943 --> 00:13:00,821
He's the leader of the Sinigang Cartel.

144
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:04,742
Do you recognize him?

145
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:15,169
You've gone up against
the Sinigang Cartel.

146
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:17,338
Eye for an eye,

147
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:19,590
tooth for a tooth.

148
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:22,426
Nose for a nose.

149
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:25,179
Wait, now I want to complete the set.

150
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:26,180
Eyebrow for an eyebrow.

151
00:13:26,847 --> 00:13:27,973
Ear for an ear.

152
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:30,226
Mole for a mole.

153
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:32,394
Hold on.

154
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:36,774
Sorry. Go on. My bad.

155
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:42,279
Going back, we want to know

156
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:45,282
if Senator Quintin is part
of the Sinigang Cartel.

157
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:52,039
See? I told you it's just a coincidence.

158
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:58,587
I can tell by the look
in your eyes that you're lying.

159
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:13,852
You might benefit too if you help us.

160
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,994
before I help you.

161
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,168
Mikoy!

162
00:14:39,169 --> 00:14:40,546
- Hey!
- Hey! Miks!

163
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:42,464
Where's Chiara?

164
00:14:43,215 --> 00:14:45,593
She's with Leonela and Alex.

165
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,428
I think they're getting ready
for the wedding.

166
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:49,805
For the wedding? What about you?

167
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:52,182
What about me?

168
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:54,476
What are you doing
to get ready for the wedding?

169
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,855
Why? Is there something I should be doing?

170
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:03,569
No offense,

171
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:06,530
but between you and Chiara,

172
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,950
you're the one who has more
preparing to do for the wedding.

173
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,368
Have you looked at yourself in the mirror?

174
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:14,997
Chiara

175
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,125
has class naturally.

176
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,128
But you…

177
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:24,381
You look like you fix
illegal electrical connections.

178
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,467
- Ouch.
- That one hurt.

179
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:29,261
You're really good at throwing insults,

180
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:31,013
but it's okay.

181
00:15:31,096 --> 00:15:32,264
I'm not offended.

182
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:35,225
I'm confident in who I am.

183
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:37,353
Confident, confident.

184
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,313
But, Mikoy,

185
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,815
this isn't about confidence.

186
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:47,947
Just imagine yourself
40 or 55 years from now.

187
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:52,660
At your wake,

188
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:56,956
like, there's a slideshow of your photos
playing on a small TV beside your casket.

189
00:15:57,581 --> 00:15:59,708
Your pictures keep flashing on the screen.

190
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:01,627
People will cringe and say,

191
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,838
"Wow, he's confident,

192
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:06,548
but he has no charm."

193
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:10,010
That's all.

194
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:14,264
So, what exactly should I do?

195
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:17,101
Wait, hold on.

196
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,478
Since we all look alike,

197
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:24,358
Come closer.

198
00:16:31,907 --> 00:16:32,825
Wait.

199
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:35,744
Is there some law that says

200
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:37,997
chicken cordon bleu has to be
on every wedding menu?

201
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:41,583
Is it a relative or something?

202
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,002
The official wedding dish?

203
00:16:44,336 --> 00:16:46,630
Nothing new? It's so cliché.

204
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:49,550
It's like…

205
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:52,052
řízek…

206
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:54,179
with cheese?

207
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,765
Yes, it has cheese.

208
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:59,852
Maybe the planner doesn't have
enough cheesiness in her own life,

209
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:01,854
so she's adding it
to someone else's wedding.

210
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:11,321
Unlike someone here
who can't stop nitpicking.

211
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:20,873
Chiara, are you chicken cordon bleu?

212
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:25,044
No, that's not the right answer.

213
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:27,296
You're supposed to say, "Why?"

214
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:28,380
Why?

215
00:17:28,464 --> 00:17:29,882
All right, let's try again.

216
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:32,551
Chiara, are you chicken cordon bleu?

217
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,678
Why?

218
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:37,931
Because no matter how cliché life gets,

219
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:40,601
just like cordon bleu,

220
00:17:40,684 --> 00:17:44,563
you're still the one
Mikoy will always long for

221
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,273
and come home to,

222
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:47,566
until the very end.

223
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:52,404
That's so corny.

224
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:55,824
Then why don't you add corn soup too,

225
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:57,993
so it matches your corny jokes?

226
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:01,538
Wow, Chiara.
Your maid of honor is something else.

227
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:04,750
She's like a real judge.
Always passing judgment.

228
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:10,172
Of course, because I only want
what's best for my friend.

229
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:25,187
Bang, bang, bang, bang, bang!

230
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:27,981
And today we're out here walking

231
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:31,902
the Kolokoys and Brother Mikoy!

232
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:34,404
- Hey!
- Yay!

233
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:36,532
So today's mission is…

234
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:40,327
Mikoy's fitting!

235
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:43,038
Bang, bang, bang!

236
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:49,503
Wait. Are we almost there?

237
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:52,089
Where exactly are we going, Captain Pepe?

238
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:53,757
You've been keeping it a secret.

239
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:56,093
So I could surprise you, of course!

240
00:18:56,176 --> 00:18:58,887
I'm sure you'll love this tailor.

241
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:00,097
He's really good!

242
00:19:00,889 --> 00:19:01,974
Why's that?

243
00:19:02,057 --> 00:19:04,643
He's an expert at making
elegant suits and barongs.

244
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:09,106
- Really?
- Making a great suit or barong

245
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:10,649
isn't about the brand.

246
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:13,902
- It's all about the fit and the fabric.
- That's it!

247
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:15,529
Wow, he really does sound good!

248
00:19:15,612 --> 00:19:17,865
- He's the real deal!
- Top-notch coats!

249
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:20,701
He makes clothes for important people.

250
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:21,910
Like who?

251
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:25,497
Mayors, barangay officers,
congressmen, governors!

252
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:27,291
None of his clients have ever complained!

253
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:29,376
- Not even one?
- Not one!

254
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:31,461
You'll be the first!

255
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:33,589
No, he's really that good.

256
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:36,383
Really? I can't wait to meet him!

257
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:38,177
Wait, what's the name of the shop?

258
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:40,179
There it is!

259
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:41,471
Libing Legend!

260
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:45,267
Come on, let me introduce you!

261
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:46,852
Come on, get inside!

262
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:47,936
Let's go!

263
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,271
Captain Pepe!

264
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,732
As your maid of honor, Chiara,

265
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:55,736
I suggest choosing either
this chocolate ganache

266
00:19:56,403 --> 00:20:00,115
or this red velvet cake
with buttercream frosting.

267
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:01,074
There.

268
00:20:01,158 --> 00:20:02,743
Simple is more authentic.

269
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:04,411
Unlike these.

270
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:07,331
That one is perfect.

271
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:10,959
Excuse me.

272
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:12,753
Last time I checked,

273
00:20:13,337 --> 00:20:15,964
you're the maid of honor,
and I'm the wedding planner.

274
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,971
You know, you're way too serious.

275
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:28,227
This isn't military duty.

276
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:31,438
I think your life's
just lacking sweetness.

277
00:20:31,521 --> 00:20:32,814
So I suggest

278
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:37,194
this layered fondant cake
should be Chiara's wedding cake.

279
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:40,030
It's classier, more aesthetic,

280
00:20:40,113 --> 00:20:42,950
and it lasts longer, just like sweetness.

281
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:45,577
Good grief. That one?

282
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:48,705
It's hard as a rock. Look at it.

283
00:20:49,748 --> 00:20:51,250
Of course it's hard. It's an iPad.

284
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:53,460
The real cake isn't that hard.

285
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:55,420
That's what we want, something that lasts.

286
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:58,006
Don't we all want forever?

287
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:00,801
That cake will outlive you.

288
00:21:00,884 --> 00:21:03,428
It could even be reused
at another wedding.

289
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:08,016
Sure, it lasts long,
but it has no life in it.

290
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,977
It's just decoration.

291
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:13,063
You might as well print a photo of a cake

292
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:15,524
and hang it at the venue.

293
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:19,236
Sounds like all you want is a stage prop.

294
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:20,404
Right, Chiara?

295
00:21:23,323 --> 00:21:24,950
You two are in your own world.

296
00:21:31,164 --> 00:21:33,417
- Layered fondant cake.
- No.

297
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,626
It's sweet and it lasts.

298
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:38,046
- No, it's hard.
- It lasts, unlike some relationships.

299
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:39,256
Unlike yours.

300
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:41,133
What's that supposed to mean?

301
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:56,940
In return,

302
00:21:59,026 --> 00:22:02,029
I asked her for a favor.

303
00:22:05,490 --> 00:22:07,284
You mean the favor I'm thinking of?

304
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:14,833
If Carlota succeeds

305
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:16,710
in carrying out the favor,

306
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:19,171
I'm sure

307
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:22,841
our story will change.

308
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:26,344
We'll be back at the top

309
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:53,914
This would look nice in your bouquet.

310
00:22:55,290 --> 00:22:56,166
No again?

311
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:58,418
It feels like every suggestion I make

312
00:22:58,502 --> 00:22:59,628
gets a "no" from you.

313
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:00,670
Hey, missy.

314
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:01,630
Hey--

315
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:03,924
Go ahead.

316
00:23:04,007 --> 00:23:05,133
- What? You can't reach it?
- You jerk!

317
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:06,927
What?

318
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:09,763
Its name is Sweet Sweet.

319
00:23:09,846 --> 00:23:10,806
Sweet Sweet?

320
00:23:11,306 --> 00:23:12,474
There's a corpse!

321
00:23:12,557 --> 00:23:14,267
There's a corpse!

322
00:23:16,895 --> 00:23:18,063
Let's eat!

323
00:23:18,146 --> 00:23:20,190
Wait, wait, wait! What are you doing?

324
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:22,776
- What else?
- You're kind of

325
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:24,277
ten kilos over the limit.

326
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:25,862
What?

327
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:36,373
- Wow!
- There…

328
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:38,375
Are you okay?

329
00:23:38,458 --> 00:23:39,668
You look so down.

330
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:45,006
Should we really do
the favor Viktor asked for?

331
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:46,967
It seems impossible.

332
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:49,386
Even I'm struggling to figure it out.

333
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:52,931
What is it that must never be revealed?
